I was in a situation similar to this. She got mad when because there were a few girls that participated in my hobbies and tried to get me to stop my hobbies. I wound up breaking up with her after she accused me of not trusting her when her friend told me that she was cheating on me (found after i broke up with her she had been cheating for weeks). After we broke up she had a tantrum blaming me for her cheating, and then she attempted suicide (found out from her friends).

&#x200B;

I'm not saying you should break up with her, but you should ask yourself, is she really worth all the friendships and sleep you are loosing? is she really the kind of person you enjoy having in your life? Are you just settling cause you are afraid of being alone? after i answered these questions it was easy to see i had to end the relationship.
